From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 23:43:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] avfilter/vf_libvmaf: pop the CUDA context when a plane copy
 fails

A failed cuMemcpy2D returns before cuCtxPopCurrent, leaving the CUDA
context current on the calling thread. This error path also exists in
upstream master at 200a98d5ba4a.

Send plane-copy failures to shared cleanup and pop once after a
successful push. Keep the copy result across a successful pop, and
return AVERROR_EXTERNAL if copying or popping fails.

Mocked CUDA-driver tests inject copy errors on each of the three planes,
plus allocation, push and pop errors. They check return values and the
context stack; successful copies at 8, 10, 12 and 16 bits check each
plane's byte width and pitch. Restoring the early return makes the
regression assertion fail. No CUDA device is required.

Signed-off-by: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
---
 libavfilter/vf_libvmaf.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libavfilter/vf_libvmaf.c b/libavfilter/vf_libvmaf.c
index 72145d2df5bc11b06377dcd9e1c0c0939b28dfac..eafb8b5671c54c9791f82bd430b367db020afd88 100644
--- a/libavfilter/vf_libvmaf.c
+++ b/libavfilter/vf_libvmaf.c
@@ -751,14 +751,14 @@ static int copy_picture_data_cuda(VmafContext* vmaf,
 
         err = cu->cuMemcpy2D(&m);
         if (err)
-            return AVERROR_EXTERNAL;
+            goto fail;
     }
 
-    err = cu->cuCtxPopCurrent(NULL);
-    if (err)
+fail:
+    if (cu->cuCtxPopCurrent(NULL))
         return AVERROR_EXTERNAL;
 
-    return 0;
+    return err ? AVERROR_EXTERNAL : 0;
 }
 
 static int do_vmaf_cuda(FFFrameSync* fs)
